   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5) — APPROVE** — head fa92234b (branch fix/852-reader-bottom-inset, before the PR)\n\nThe cause is right for #852 and #641: `.ignoresSafeArea(edges: .vertical)` applied to the `GeometryReader` itself put its proxy outside the safe area, so `obscured` was zero at both edges. `ReaderUnderBars` reads the real insets, then moves the ignore onto the content. The bottom controls are `.bottomBar` toolbar items (`ReaderPageControls.swift:21`), part of the child's safe area. The top `.safeAreaInset` banners now count. No compile issue found.\n\n1. **minor** — `ReaderWebView.swift:31`: the outer `GeometryReader` now respects the keyboard region. With the partial-height composer open over the reader, `obscured.bottom` may jump by the keyboard height. Fix: `.ignoresSafeArea(.keyboard)` on the reader, plus a check with the composer open.\n2. **minor** — `ReaderUnderBarsTests.swift:15`: the test covers the wrapper only. Say in the PR how it was seen red; keep `Refs #641`.\n3. **nit** — `ReaderUnderBarsTests.swift:22-26`: hide the test window at the end.\n4. **nit** — Other edge cases (hidden bars, landscape, page turn) move the insets as expected; a quick device check is enough.\n\nVerified: the diff, TopicReaderView, ReaderPageControls, ReaderWebView, ReaderWebController (+Scroll), ReaderScrollGeometry, ReaderReplyFlow, ComposerHeight, #852, #641. No build or run.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
