   "body": "**Adversarial review round 2 (Opus 5.5) — APPROVE** — head 12f716b2 (round 1: APPROVE with minors at fa92234b)\n\n`.ignoresSafeArea(.keyboard)` removes only the keyboard region (edges `.all`): the container safe area (navigation bar, `.bottomBar` page controls, the top `.safeAreaInset` banner, home indicator) stays in `proxy.safeAreaInsets`, the keyboard's does not, and the reader no longer shrinks when the keyboard opens. It is the outermost layout modifier of `ReaderUnderBars.body`, so it acts. This matches the old code (all regions ignored vertically; horizontal container insets still respected).\n\n1. **nit** — `ReaderUnderBarsTests.swift:15`: no test covers the keyboard (a hosted test cannot raise one reliably). Note a device check with the composer and its keyboard open in the PR.\n2. Round-1 points settled: the `defer` hides the window on every exit; the comment at `ReaderWebView.swift:34` is accurate.\n\nNo regression in the branch diff.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
